{title: More Than Watchmen Wait}
{subtitle: Psalms 130:5–6}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] [Bb/F] | [Eb] |
| [Fsus4] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Lord, hear my [F/A]voice as I [Gm7]call to you
[Eb]Let your ears be atten[Fsus4]tive to my cry
[Bb]If you kept a re[F/A]cord of my [Gm7]sins
Who could [Eb]stand before [Fsus4]you?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I [Bb]wait for the Lord, [F/A]my soul [Gm7]waits
[Eb]And in his word I put [Fsus4]my hope
My [Bb]soul waits [F/A]for the [Gm7]Lord
More [Eb]than watchmen [Fsus4]wait for the morn[Bb]ing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But with [F/A]you there is for[Gm7]giveness
[Eb]So that you may be [Fsus4]feared
I [Bb]wait for the Lord, [F/A]my soul [Gm7]waits
[Eb]And in his word I put [Fsus4]my hope
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Israel, hope in the [Gm7]Lord
For with the [Bb]Lord there is stead[Fsus4]fast love
With [Eb]him is abundant re[Gm7]demption
He him[Bb]self will redeem Israel from [Fsus4]all their sins
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
My soul waits [F/A]for the [Gm7]Lord
More than [Eb]watchmen [Fsus4]wait for the morn[Bb]ing
{end_of_verse}
